# ad09 — Guest Scout: a real agent doing a real job (hero cut, 78s)
# Edit plan: marketing/assets/videos/guest-scout-real-run.md
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:08.0]
This is not a staged demo. A real automation on a real Instagram account, finding podcast guests.

[00:08.0 --> 00:20.0]
First move: it reads its own last shortlist -- marked partial -- so this pass hunts only for NEW candidates. The task is a file; the state is a file too.

[00:20.0 --> 00:38.0]
The pane becomes a real browser inside the desktop app. Discovery only -- it never follows, likes, or messages. And it narrates its own reasoning as it reads the feed: promising leads, worth investigating.

[00:38.0 --> 00:52.0]
Dead end? It corrects itself -- pivots to a profile it already trusts and mines the similar-accounts graph instead. Nobody is steering.

[00:52.0 --> 01:04.0]
All on a leash: three books of budget per pass, a wrap-up leg at ninety percent, and an LLM judge that decides when the shortlist is done.

[01:04.0 --> 01:12.0]
The output isn't a chat transcript. It's a shortlist file -- merged, de-duplicated, versioned.

[01:12.0 --> 01:18.0]
Agents that work while you sleep. rysh dot A I.
